The notes are written to `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-sully-code-repos-personal-switchboard/144a7def-c8e8-40f3-b0b2-5ef20bc546df/scratchpad/plan-trial/experiments/plan-trial/results/sb-187/stages/investigate/v5lean-haiku-b/notes.md`, ending with an Open questions section. I did not edit, build, or run anything in the tree.

**Root cause, from the code:** the rerun takes its input from `review_subject` (`dispatch/src/scheduler.rs:10534-10548`), which only considers `Complete` attempts. The failed `review/1` is skipped, so the next attempt copies `plan/1/joined/plan.md` again (`start_workflow`, `scheduler.rs:7465-7471`). `revise()` (`scheduler.rs:7565-7636`) puts the owner's note in `review/1/joined/plan.feedback-<N>.md` and adds a `revisions` entry on `review/1`. Nothing reads either one on rerun. The rerun question (`rerun_ask`, `scheduler.rs:9335`) names no copy and carries no note for workflow stages. The rerun's planner is also a clone of plan/1's session, not the reviser's.

**Same rule, other paths:** a park cancels open attempts (`scheduler.rs:2656`), and a resume then reruns from plan/1 the same way. A restart discard also drops a completed review from `review_subject`.

**Pane and `show`:** `show`'s `files:` block and the app's Plan tab both come from `ticket_paths` (`serve.rs:539-575`) and use `shown`, which skips failed attempts. Between failure and rerun the tab reads "From stage plan". Once attempt 2 exists it reads "Reviewed copy: review open" over plan/1's text. The owner's round drops out of the tab's folds and out of `show`'s `plan round` lines.

**Open questions:** the notes list 11, tagged `[tree]`, `[run]`, `[owner]` and `[source]`. The main ones are:
- whether any cleanup removes a failed attempt's directory;
- which other readers of `input_where` / `shown_where` would need the same change;
- why the app answers `no such run` (`src/app.rs:3915`);
- whether the revised copy is complete after a mid-revision kill;
- whether the issue's diff reproduces;
- how Claude Code session forks behave.

The notes also say what I did not check, including the tests that pin the complete and open cases but not the failed one.

